{"explanation": "The unit is most active on small, long-haired toy and terrier breeds (Maltese, Shih-Tzu, Lhasa, Yorkshire, silky terrier and similar) and on other furry faces such as the lesser panda and meerkat. On the first photos it looked strongly selective for right-facing subjects (row 1) and for centered rather than right-third subjects (row 8). Neither held on new photos (percentiles 80 and 67), so those were probably sample noise. Its preference for right-facing over frontal subjects (row 3) was about the same on both sets, at the 92nd and 91st percentiles, and its similar units did not share it. That makes it a weak tendency particular to this unit, but it never reached the unusual range. The preferences for frontal over left-facing subjects, large frame fill and sharpness are shared with the similar units. No row is reliably both strong and specific to this unit.", "rows": []}
